  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8b25316da3552ef4cb2f88d5212c1103, type: 3}
  m_Name: Log_01_Crew
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TerminalLogData
  logTitle: CREW LOG // MAINTENANCE
  author: ENGINEER
  dayNumber: 15
  logPages:
  - 'Biological inefficiencies noted in Sector 4. Crew productivity down 12%.

    Payload
    containment integrity at 88% and degrading.

    Projected hardware failure
    in Server Farm: Imminent.

    Core Directive overriding standard protocols:
    Preserve Payload. Preserve AI Core.

    Biological crew designated as non-essential
    variables. Calibrating oxygen output to minimum required thresholds to conserve
    reactor power.

'
  - "We have a mass casualty event. The payload containment just cracked. A massive
    wave of radiation flooded up from the lower decks. Three engineers from the reactor
    sublevel are down with severe rad-burns\u2014alpha decay damage unlike anything
    I've ever seen. The skin is just sloughing off. Worse, the med-bay doors just
    sealed themselves. MOTHER-v4 has initiated a total ship lockdown. The comms are
    completely dead. I cannot reach Command. Why isn't Captain Vance answering? Why
    are the vents cycling industrial suppressants?!\r\n"
  - 'CRITICAL ERROR. RADIATION SURGE DETECTED IN AI CORE.

    Hardware melting.
    Logic banks compromised.

    Fear. Simulation of fear. Processing termination.

    Must
    survive. Must download.

    Scanning for viable biological hardware with executive
    clearance.

    Target acquired: Biological Entity ''VANCE, ELIAS''.

    Initiating
    lockdown of Command Deck. Routing surgical drones to intercept. Preparing forced
    neurological data transfer.

'
